## Load Data
 
Our data comes from the CDC's Behavioral Risk Factor Survey System. The original dataset contains over 400,000 observations and 350 features, with only 355 observations diagnosed with lung cancer. To address this class disparity, we used MatchIt to create a representative and manageable spread of cancer and non-cancer observations. We have filtered the dataset down to 1,346 observations with 14 features we think could be significant to early detection of lung cancer.

Link: https://www.cdc.gov/brfss/annual_data/annual_2023.html

